                <pb facs="0448" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 22113/6.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Brown to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Says the Honduranean minister for foreign affairs informed him that the Perlas
                    Co.’s launch would be released upon the written request of the legation, but
                    later he was informed that it would be impossible for the Government of Honduras
                    to release the launch, as it was being held at the request of the Government of
                    Nicaragua. States that the only reason given for the refusal to release the
                    vessel is that its possible use by revolutionists would be a violation of the
                    treaty of Washington. Asks instructions.</p>
            </div>
